                "reply_count": 2,
                "retweet_count": 4,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "I sat down with @repmcgovern and leaders in the nutrition space in East Oakland for a conversation on rising food insecurity after the Republicans passed the largest cut to SNAP in history with their budget bill. Republicans are trying to break our social safety net, but we are linking arms to work together, create our own solutions, and lift up our people. We can end hunger, we can end poverty -- but we can't do that if we pathologize the poor, willingly let people fall through the cracks, and refuse to create actual conditions that allow people to work and succeed.\n\nWhen I return to Washington in September for committee work and votes in Congress, I am carrying the wisdom and insight shared here today by our community leaders, nonprofit leaders, and philahtorphy leaders back as I work to combat Republican\u2019s assault on the American people.",
